{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1867, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array cost of size n. You are currently at position n (at the end of the line) in a line of n + 1 people (numbered from 0 to n).\nYou wish to move forward in the line, but each person in front of you charges a specific amount to swap places. The cost to swap with person i is given by cost[i].\nYou are allowed to swap places with people as follows:\n\nIf they are in front of you, you must pay them cost[i] to swap with them.\nIf they are behind you, they can swap with you for free.\n\nReturn an array answer of size n, where answer[i] is the minimum total cost to reach each position i in the line.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: cost = [5,3,4,1,3,2]\nOutput: [5,3,3,1,1,1]\nExplanation:\nWe can get to each position in the following way:\n\ni = 0. We can swap with person 0 for a cost of 5.\ni = 1. We can swap with person 1 for a cost of 3.\ni = 2. We can swap with person 1 for a cost of 3, then swap with person 2 for free.\ni = 3. We can swap with person 3 for a cost of 1.\ni = 4. We can swap with person 3 for a cost of 1, then swap with person 4 for free.\ni = 5. We can swap with person 3 for a cost of 1, then swap with person 5 for free.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: cost = [1,2,4,6,7]\nOutput: [1,1,1,1,1]\nExplanation:\nWe can swap with person 0 for a cost of 1, then we will be able to reach any position i for free.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= n == cost.length <= 100\n1 <= cost[i] <= 100\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def minCosts(self, cost: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1931, "char_start": 1879, "quote": "Input:\n[5, 3, 4, 1, 3, 2]\nOutput:\n[5, 3, 3, 1, 1, 1]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1989, "char_start": 1943, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 4, 6, 7]\nOutput:\n[1, 1, 1, 1, 1]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "3f283b3f1ed4499caffb2274ceab389bce66139d419b4968c9aa4bd69e7885ad", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "2125e69e3c04b853cbc02d3ac429210b0cc153b19240afbacd14109822e88db9", "seq": 2}
